WEBVTT

00:01:39.120 --> 00:01:42.040
Impossible! The Führer was one of those monsters?

00:01:42.330 --> 00:01:43.900
Orders, ma'am? What about the attack?

00:01:43.900 --> 00:01:45.540
We haven't received instructions. Hold for now.

00:01:50.950 --> 00:01:52.250
Wait! Stop!

00:01:52.250 --> 00:01:55.310
What are you doing? Fire at them already!

00:01:55.310 --> 00:01:57.950
Look at that live feed! Something strange is happening!

00:01:57.950 --> 00:01:59.230
What live feed?

00:01:59.230 --> 00:02:00.350
Switch your drones to standby mode!

00:02:07.450 --> 00:02:09.020
The enemy's withdrawing?

00:02:16.600 --> 00:02:20.030
<i>This is unfortunate. What is the Council going to do about this?!</i>

00:02:20.840 --> 00:02:22.780
L-Let go of His Excellency!

00:02:22.780 --> 00:02:27.040
Stand down! This is not someone who deserves your oath of loyalty!

00:02:27.040 --> 00:02:28.480
It's war!

00:02:27.040 --> 00:02:28.480
What about those students, then?

00:02:28.480 --> 00:02:30.170
Like you can believe anything Dorssia says.

00:02:28.480 --> 00:02:30.170
It's Dorssian soldiers who are behind this!

00:02:30.440 --> 00:02:33.610
If the Führer himself is one of these dangerous lifeforms,

00:02:33.610 --> 00:02:35.670
how can anything Dorssia does be trusted?

00:02:35.670 --> 00:02:37.070
I don't believe it...

00:02:37.070 --> 00:02:38.880
How much of what he said is true?

00:02:38.880 --> 00:02:40.160
We did it!

00:02:40.160 --> 00:02:41.550
Not much fun, is it, you Dorssian bastards?!

00:02:41.800 --> 00:02:43.740
This will turn the tide!

00:02:43.740 --> 00:02:45.930
This also spells the end of the Dorssio-ARUS alliance, doesn't it?

00:02:46.320 --> 00:02:50.190
Can we go back to school, now?

00:02:50.510 --> 00:02:51.560
Of course!

00:02:52.680 --> 00:02:54.730
That all depends on what stance the ARUS takes after this, though.

00:02:54.730 --> 00:02:58.780
Things look bad for Dorssia. Looks like a civil war's inevitable.

00:02:59.070 --> 00:03:01.840
We staked it all on one roll of the dice, and that turned the tables!

00:03:01.840 --> 00:03:04.030
We made it, Yamada!

00:03:08.320 --> 00:03:11.290
We did it! We did it, Yamada!

00:03:19.610 --> 00:03:20.260
It's fast!

00:03:24.690 --> 00:03:25.640
What the—

00:03:26.030 --> 00:03:27.280
What's going on?

00:03:39.360 --> 00:03:41.070
You lowly Valvrave knockoff.

00:03:51.740 --> 00:03:52.670
Akira!

00:03:52.910 --> 00:03:54.540
Cain, Pino is in there!

00:03:54.960 --> 00:03:58.050
Prue, I'm going to fulfill my promise to you now.

00:04:05.430 --> 00:04:08.760
What's going on? Things were just getting good!

00:04:09.970 --> 00:04:13.820
According to reports we've just received, the scene we just witnessed

00:04:13.820 --> 00:04:16.980
was doctored by type seven dangerous lifeforms.

00:04:17.320 --> 00:04:21.240
So it was all a ploy by those students? Or rather, those monsters?

00:04:21.240 --> 00:04:23.450
What the hell, it was fake?!

00:04:23.450 --> 00:04:25.070
See, what did I tell you?

00:04:24.280 --> 00:04:25.900
Boy, what a relief!

00:04:25.070 --> 00:04:27.240
So those students are the only monsters, then?

00:04:28.130 --> 00:04:29.620
Why did that happen?

00:04:29.950 --> 00:04:32.160
They probably leaned on the media behind the scenes.

00:04:32.160 --> 00:04:33.620
This quickly?!

00:04:34.040 --> 00:04:38.000
This means that we can't just slug it out with these people.

00:04:38.380 --> 00:04:41.820
Give them doctored footage to analyze and have them lend credence to the story.

00:04:41.820 --> 00:04:44.510
For the time being, the situation appears to be quieting down.

00:04:44.830 --> 00:04:50.010
Magius are in their shadows, and all is right with the world.

00:04:50.490 --> 00:04:56.440
The Council of the Hundred and One is composed of the world's most influential people.

00:04:56.980 --> 00:05:02.030
How many incidents and accidents do you think we have arranged over the centuries?

00:05:19.170 --> 00:05:21.630
It's powerful... This is Unit 2?

00:05:35.290 --> 00:05:38.150
Cain! This is for H-Neun!

00:05:47.200 --> 00:05:51.580
Now it makes sense. L-Elf's infiltration was your handiwork, wasn't it?

00:06:03.170 --> 00:06:06.890
They're fighting each other? Did L-Elf set this up?

00:06:08.100 --> 00:06:10.050
Don't! Stay back, Akira!

00:06:10.050 --> 00:06:10.940
But...

00:06:10.940 --> 00:06:12.560
You're too heavily damaged to do anything!

00:06:15.060 --> 00:06:17.180
X, don't run off ahead by yourself!

00:06:21.650 --> 00:06:25.570
Well, our little prince became a turncoat...

00:06:25.570 --> 00:06:26.690
Q-Vier!

00:06:26.990 --> 00:06:30.240
Valvraves and now the Perfection Army.

00:06:30.240 --> 00:06:32.200
It's a veritable feast today!

00:06:33.200 --> 00:06:34.700
Thank goodness you're all right, Mr. President!

00:06:35.080 --> 00:06:38.500
ARUS forces are currently keeping their distance from the ongoing Valvrave battle.

00:06:38.500 --> 00:06:41.290
Assemble all staff officers aboard my flagship!

00:06:41.290 --> 00:06:44.090
All forces are to cease hostilities until we reach a decision!

00:07:05.390 --> 00:07:08.150
That unit can do things that mine can't?!

00:07:14.370 --> 00:07:15.690
I can still fight!

00:07:15.690 --> 00:07:17.370
This is no time to be holding back!

00:07:22.460 --> 00:07:24.710
I can still fight! I can fight!

00:07:39.230 --> 00:07:43.600
The pilot is more competent than before, but still not enough.

00:07:51.530 --> 00:07:54.280
Readiness evaluation, D.

00:07:58.530 --> 00:08:00.200
Stop this, Q-Vier!

00:08:01.340 --> 00:08:03.870
It was Cain who killed H-Neun!

00:08:04.360 --> 00:08:08.670
So what if he did? Killing a traitor is a good thing!

00:08:10.680 --> 00:08:12.340
Hear me out!

00:08:12.680 --> 00:08:16.600
"Death to traitors." That's what we swore, remember?

00:08:17.220 --> 00:08:20.600
I'm just happy to get the chance to fight someone tough!

00:08:26.610 --> 00:08:27.690
Cain!

00:08:30.650 --> 00:08:31.690
You'll pay!

00:08:32.140 --> 00:08:36.570
You betrayed H-Neun! And my trust!

00:08:36.910 --> 00:08:41.330
Sacrificing oneself for one's friends is noble. I don't begrudge you that.

00:08:41.920 --> 00:08:43.330
At point blank...

00:08:43.330 --> 00:08:46.500
It'll be worth dying if I can take you with me!

00:09:05.390 --> 00:09:09.580
An attack you staked your life on. Brilliantly played, X-Ein.

00:09:10.120 --> 00:09:11.980
I'll give you a readiness evaluation of A.

00:09:17.240 --> 00:09:18.660
H-Neun,

00:09:19.400 --> 00:09:23.870
if you were in my place, I know you'd be cracking wise...

00:09:36.660 --> 00:09:37.880
Tokishima Haruto!

00:09:38.680 --> 00:09:41.760
A novice in combat training stands no chance to defeat Cain!

00:09:44.800 --> 00:09:47.650
Maybe not, but I have to try!

00:09:47.650 --> 00:09:50.580
My point is that I will fight with you.

00:09:51.470 --> 00:09:55.790
I have reasons to defeat him that surpass even yours.

00:09:55.790 --> 00:09:57.110
So use me.

00:09:57.580 --> 00:09:59.370
Oh, right! I can hijack your body!

00:09:59.710 --> 00:10:03.870
Between my body, which has had combat techniques drilled into it, and your curse...

00:10:04.190 --> 00:10:05.620
We can do it together!

00:10:17.400 --> 00:10:19.390
All right, let's wrap this up, shall we?

00:10:35.690 --> 00:10:38.030
This speed and sword technique...

00:10:39.120 --> 00:10:40.410
Is that you, L-Elf?

00:10:40.410 --> 00:10:42.410
We're still alive!

00:10:42.410 --> 00:10:45.040
We won't be silenced by you!

00:10:54.470 --> 00:10:59.680
You know, Haruto, when I heard that your memories were disappearing,

00:10:59.680 --> 00:11:01.180
I was actually looking forward to it a little.

00:11:01.680 --> 00:11:04.890
I mean, who can compete against a childhood friend?

00:11:05.360 --> 00:11:09.860
If you lost your memories, I'd be on an even footing with her.

00:11:10.900 --> 00:11:12.940
I'm a horrible person, aren't I?

00:11:13.720 --> 00:11:15.400
The JIORan Module is moving!

00:11:15.400 --> 00:11:19.520
A Valvrave! There's more left!

00:11:19.520 --> 00:11:20.320
Q-Vier!

00:11:20.680 --> 00:11:22.740
Cannon fire has been forbidden!

00:11:22.740 --> 00:11:25.680
Don't forget that we have important people in there.

00:11:25.680 --> 00:11:29.750
Two Kirschbaums are en route. Lieutenants A-Drei and Q-Vier!

00:11:30.400 --> 00:11:33.750
<i>A-drei... I can't offer you any direct support.</i>

00:11:36.120 --> 00:11:39.290
I know that Haruto will choose Shoko,

00:11:39.290 --> 00:11:42.490
but I promised myself that I wouldn't give up.

00:11:55.150 --> 00:11:56.650
Hostilities have been suspended!

00:11:56.650 --> 00:11:59.940
I'll deal with you after I take out that Valvrave!

00:12:18.620 --> 00:12:22.510
So that's why he'd been using a Waffe's shield...

00:12:24.760 --> 00:12:27.720
Well done, A-Drei...

00:12:28.720 --> 00:12:30.770
I knew you'd be tough!

00:12:31.080 --> 00:12:32.520
Q-Vier...

00:12:32.840 --> 00:12:35.800
I knew you'd be the best...

00:12:36.870 --> 00:12:38.820
You're so cool...

00:13:00.830 --> 00:13:03.100
You understand nothing.

00:13:03.760 --> 00:13:08.300
The Council of the Hundred and One is no evil secret society.

00:13:08.730 --> 00:13:12.180
We are champions of justice who safeguard the peace of the world.

00:13:12.180 --> 00:13:14.690
You're saying the Council members are the good guys?!

00:13:14.690 --> 00:13:18.520
Humans were the ones to attack first!

00:13:19.200 --> 00:13:24.030
We desired only coexistence, but humanity feared and attacked us.

00:13:24.730 --> 00:13:29.530
Legends of supernatural monsters around the world are a chronicle of Magius suffering!

00:13:29.530 --> 00:13:33.000
It is for that reason that we, over the course of many years,

00:13:33.000 --> 00:13:35.770
made deals with the world's leading figures.

00:13:35.770 --> 00:13:40.080
We Magius have lived in secret so as not to arouse the fear of humanity.

00:13:40.080 --> 00:13:41.550
And in return...

00:13:41.800 --> 00:13:45.670
...they tacitly allow us to prey upon a certain number of humans!

00:13:46.080 --> 00:13:51.430
It is only because of the Council system that humanity has been kept safe from fear and chaos!

00:13:51.430 --> 00:13:55.060
In short, the ones who threaten the peace and order of the world

00:13:55.400 --> 00:13:58.120
are you people and your Valvraves!

00:13:58.920 --> 00:14:00.520
That's your excuse?!

00:14:05.450 --> 00:14:09.180
Did we do the right thing?

00:14:09.180 --> 00:14:11.950
You saw it! You saw how Tokishima Haruto didn't die!

00:14:11.950 --> 00:14:16.710
I did. But I didn't see him killing your father, Iori.

00:14:21.170 --> 00:14:23.090
Let's go find out.

00:14:24.230 --> 00:14:26.900
Teach, are you okay?

00:14:26.900 --> 00:14:31.570
It's at times like this when a teacher has to stand up.

00:14:31.570 --> 00:14:34.090
Find out? Find out how?

00:14:34.690 --> 00:14:38.230
We'll talk. That's all.

00:14:38.730 --> 00:14:44.780
The thing about the truth is, you'll never know what it is unless you come out and ask.

00:14:51.490 --> 00:14:55.240
Stop it, big brother! I don't hate this human!

00:14:55.240 --> 00:15:01.830
I can't do that! He's one of the people who locked us up in these machines to try to use us as a power source!

00:15:07.670 --> 00:15:09.680
No! We're leaking runes!

00:15:18.810 --> 00:15:22.440
Can't we... win against him?

00:15:22.440 --> 00:15:27.440
We walked hand in hand with history, were hurt, and came to a realization.

00:15:27.820 --> 00:15:32.530
A system where there could be no conflict between us meant living separately.

00:15:33.200 --> 00:15:35.390
Very well, let's put an end to this.

00:15:35.390 --> 00:15:38.700
I'll eliminate you two and reclaim our peace!

00:15:41.710 --> 00:15:43.330
We're coming, Pino!

00:15:45.840 --> 00:15:46.880
You're wrong!

00:15:49.490 --> 00:15:50.300
What's that?

00:15:50.300 --> 00:15:53.680
Did you consider trying to live together with humanity, too?

00:15:53.680 --> 00:15:56.670
You gave up because you'd been hurt.

00:15:57.600 --> 00:16:00.570
You built a wall of lies so neither would hurt the other.

00:16:01.190 --> 00:16:06.820
He was my friend even after he lost his guiding light,

00:16:06.820 --> 00:16:09.560
and picked himself up to make her dream a reality!

00:16:10.590 --> 00:16:14.450
And the girl that I love, even after losing her father,

00:16:14.450 --> 00:16:17.580
even though he was the prime minister, she kept on fighting!

00:16:18.290 --> 00:16:21.040
Its power is increasing?

00:16:21.040 --> 00:16:25.820
For all of our friends who haven't given up even after being hurt again and again,

00:16:25.820 --> 00:16:27.540
we can't lose to you!

00:16:32.120 --> 00:16:33.800
A coup?!

00:16:33.800 --> 00:16:35.470
Now, of all times?

00:16:35.870 --> 00:16:38.030
Conflict is sparking in at least seven locations.

00:16:38.030 --> 00:16:40.720
They're breaking out simultaneously all across Dorssian territory.

00:16:41.450 --> 00:16:44.230
We Royalists have long awaited the right time to take action.

00:16:44.920 --> 00:16:48.880
Regardless of the veracity of the information brought to us by the boy named L-Elf,

00:16:48.880 --> 00:16:50.730
it provides sufficient pretext.

00:16:50.730 --> 00:16:54.820
Yes, Excellency. This is a golden opportunity for the Royalists to rise up and turn the tables.

00:16:54.820 --> 00:16:57.700
Hey, that's the president of the Winkers Company!

00:16:55.750 --> 00:16:57.700
Looks like a list of those monsters.

00:16:57.700 --> 00:16:59.260
What in the world is this?

00:16:59.260 --> 00:17:00.440
This is a hoax!

00:17:00.440 --> 00:17:02.830
Perhaps, but some of it is true!

00:17:03.130 --> 00:17:05.560
It is not a problem. We will deal with it.

00:17:05.560 --> 00:17:06.730
New information, sir!

00:17:06.730 --> 00:17:08.880
The president of the Global Bank has been taken into custody!

00:17:08.880 --> 00:17:11.380
Preposterous! He isn't a member of the Council!

00:17:15.200 --> 00:17:17.760
They're being whipped into a frenzy by some made-up stories?!

00:17:18.370 --> 00:17:20.720
Targets have been apprehended.

00:17:20.720 --> 00:17:23.520
Was it wise to trust that list, sir?

00:17:23.950 --> 00:17:28.520
Our only option is to take action now! Before the monsters can band together!

00:17:29.070 --> 00:17:32.900
<i>If we play this right, we might be able to get rid of the Magius.</i>

00:17:33.310 --> 00:17:37.600
We don't want a future that was given up on and closed off from the very beginning!

00:17:37.600 --> 00:17:38.410
I mean...

00:17:41.410 --> 00:17:45.000
...our friends never gave up, so I can't, either!

00:17:45.000 --> 00:17:47.750
You stupid boy who knows nothing of history!

00:17:59.590 --> 00:18:01.100
I'll do it!

00:18:33.710 --> 00:18:34.710
Prue!

00:18:50.230 --> 00:18:51.730
It's all over!

00:19:03.740 --> 00:19:05.740
Cain! Cain!

00:19:06.920 --> 00:19:08.250
Prue...

00:19:57.820 --> 00:19:58.900
Tokishima Haruto!

00:19:59.440 --> 00:20:01.660
We've done it! We've won!

00:20:03.550 --> 00:20:09.180
Haruto? Is that my name?

00:20:15.520 --> 00:20:18.190
He used up all his runes.

00:20:21.130 --> 00:20:25.060
I don't understand any of this.

00:20:26.210 --> 00:20:28.330
Where am I?

00:20:29.680 --> 00:20:31.600
Who are you?

00:20:31.600 --> 00:20:34.780
You don't remember? Anything at all?

00:20:36.790 --> 00:20:38.730
Not even our contract?

00:20:40.950 --> 00:20:43.610
Our fight on the Moon?

00:20:44.580 --> 00:20:45.770
Sorry.

00:20:48.370 --> 00:20:50.010
You and I, we...

00:20:55.190 --> 00:20:59.300
You know me, don't you?

00:21:00.280 --> 00:21:02.040
You know who I am?

00:21:04.920 --> 00:21:08.580
Yes, you're...

00:21:11.590 --> 00:21:13.460
You are my friend.

00:21:30.070 --> 00:21:31.850
Imperial Calendar, year 0.

00:21:32.400 --> 00:21:37.350
This would later be known as the year the Third Galactic Empire began,

00:21:37.780 --> 00:21:43.610
but it goes without saying that we never could have imagined that at the time.

00:21:44.190 --> 00:21:47.540
Afterwards, pandemonium broke out across the world.

00:21:48.680 --> 00:21:53.770
Seeing monsters everywhere, people sought out Magius all over the world,

00:21:52.290 --> 00:21:54.790
Begone

00:21:52.290 --> 00:21:54.790
magius

00:21:52.290 --> 00:21:54.790
Take Your

00:21:52.290 --> 00:21:54.790
punishment

00:21:53.770 --> 00:21:59.420
and eventually, neither the Council of the Hundred and One nor the existence of Magius could remain hidden.

00:21:59.420 --> 00:22:01.210
They found a Magius!

00:22:00.140 --> 00:22:02.880
This one's for real this time, right?

00:22:01.210 --> 00:22:02.880
Just how many are there?

00:22:02.880 --> 00:22:07.930
I think it was because the world had become too connected for secrets to be kept.

00:22:11.940 --> 00:22:15.920
Shoko cried her eyes out. It felt like an eternity.

00:22:19.320 --> 00:22:23.440
After a while, she went back to being her usual self.

00:22:24.380 --> 00:22:25.860
But every once in a while...

00:22:31.760 --> 00:22:36.140
In any case, we found ourselves a place to call home.

00:22:53.320 --> 00:22:57.400
Our Galactic Empire started from such a tiny country?

00:22:57.400 --> 00:23:01.180
Historical beginnings are often surprisingly humble.

00:23:02.820 --> 00:23:04.400
Th-There's an emergency!

00:23:04.780 --> 00:23:09.780
There's an intruder in the Memorial Core! It's supposed to be lifeform 53s!

00:23:22.690 --> 00:23:24.670
What were you expecting, a secret weapon?

00:23:26.680 --> 00:23:30.340
These are the statues of the heroes we call "The First Knights".

00:23:31.360 --> 00:23:35.830
People who were dear to me who died one by one when we founded this country.

00:23:37.810 --> 00:23:39.740
Let's try to be friends.

00:23:40.440 --> 00:23:43.320
I won't pretend that that will suddenly solve everything.

00:23:44.320 --> 00:23:49.420
But if we do, we'll be able to take all our pain and joy and go halfsies!
